From: Robert Senderek <robert.senderek@10g.pl>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:19:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: remove the 800 MHz OPP

Retain the 1008 MHz operating point and CPUFreq integration. Only remove
the lower OPP; do not describe this as disabling the whole CPUFreq driver.

Signed-off-by: Robert Senderek <robert.senderek@10g.pl>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -95,12 +95,6 @@
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 		opp-shared;
 
-		opp-800000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <800000000>;
-			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
-			clock-latency-ns = <200000>;
-		};
-
 		opp-1008000000 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1008000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
